[img]IMG_BASE/title.png[/img]
ZeD-GUI replaces the inventory, the character and loot windows, the HUD and the menus for Build 42. The style is based on a 1993 Mac. It works with a controller and with a mouse and keyboard.

[img]IMG_BASE/hero.jpg[/img]

[img]IMG_BASE/h_before_you_subscribe.png[/img]
[list]
[*][b]Build 42 only.[/b] Tested on 42.21. It does not run on Build 41.
[*][b]Tested in single player.[/b] It has not been tested in multiplayer. If you try it on a server, report what happened.
[*][b]It replaces the game's inventory and character windows.[/b] Buttons that other mods add to those windows do not show while ZeD-GUI is on. Mods that use the game's own systems (context menu options, container buttons, items, recipes) work. The compatibility discussion has the list.
[*][b]It adds one item:[/b] a steel digital watch in the loot. If you remove ZeD-GUI from a save, those watches are removed too. Everything else is interface and can be added or removed at any time.
[*][b]Text is in English.[/b] Where the game already has a word or phrase, ZeD-GUI uses the game's translation. ZeD-GUI's own text is in one file for translators.
[/list]

[img]IMG_BASE/h_windows.png[/img]
[b]Character window.[/b] Tabs for loot, equipment, health, temperature, ID, journal, skills and the radio you carry.

[b]World window.[/b] Tabs for loot, crafting (at a bench or station near you), building, furniture, maps, foraging, animals, radios nearby and the vehicle you are next to.

Open containers show as columns side by side. Either window's side panel can be rolled up into its title bar.

[img]IMG_BASE/stocking_shelves.jpg[/img]

[b]Cards.[/b] Click an item, a generator, a campfire, a farm plot, a trough, a padlock or a liquid to open its card. The card lists what it is, the actions you can take and the reason an action is not available.

[img]IMG_BASE/item_cards.jpg[/img]

[img]IMG_BASE/h_hud.png[/img]
[list]
[*][b]Belt:[/b] your hands, and the attachment slots of the gear you wear, on a strap drawn in the gear's material.
[*][b]Watch:[/b] a worn watch shows on the belt. Click it for the full watch: time, date, temperature, alarm and stopwatch.
[*][b]Dashboard:[/b] shows when you drive. The radio in the dashboard opens up close.
[*][b]Moodles:[/b] placed right, left or above the belt.
[*][b]Action bar:[/b] shows the current action and the queue in words, or as ten segments.
[/list]

[img]IMG_BASE/smoke_break.jpg[/img]

[img]IMG_BASE/h_maps.png[/img]
Three styles: survey, color and a paper road map. Flyers you have read are pinned on the map. Notes use the game's map notes, so they also show on the game's map.

[img]IMG_BASE/the_route.jpg[/img]

[img]IMG_BASE/h_menus.png[/img]
The main menu is a desk with a monitor. Load, new game, mods, options, sandbox, character creation and server settings open as windows on the monitor. They use the game's own menu functions. Mods lists conflicts between mods (two mods changing the same file, item or recipe) and which one loads last.

[img]IMG_BASE/desk.jpg[/img]

[img]IMG_BASE/h_controller.png[/img]
The controller scheme was designed by a player who plays on a controller.
[list]
[*]The D-pad moves between controls. A is left click, B is right click. X and Y open menus.
[*]Aiming with the right stick hides both windows at once and returns control to the game. Press Y to show them again.
[*]Camera zoom is a bumper chord: hold one bumper and tap the other. Hold LB and tap RB to zoom out. Hold RB and tap LB to zoom in. Each tap is one step.
[*]Map: RT zooms in, LT zooms out. The left stick moves the cursor, and pushing it to an edge pans the map.
[*]If your Steam Input layout binds the bumpers to zoom, remove those bindings. ZeD-GUI handles the zoom itself.
[/list]

[img]IMG_BASE/customers.jpg[/img]

[img]IMG_BASE/h_options.png[/img]
Dark, light or high contrast theme, nine accent colors, two text sizes, and a UI scale setting. Auto picks the scale from the screen height.

[img]IMG_BASE/themes.jpg[/img]

[img]IMG_BASE/h_getting_started.png[/img]
[olist]
[*]Subscribe.
[*]Main menu, Mods: turn on [b]ZeD-GUI[/b]. Put it after other interface mods in the load order.
[*]Start or continue a game.
[*]Options, Mods, ZeD-GUI: set the theme, accent, text size, scale, moodle position and action bar.
[*]The inventory key opens the Character window. The loot key opens the World window. Controller buttons are the same as in the game.
[/olist]

[img]IMG_BASE/h_reporting_a_problem.png[/img]
Post in the [b]Bug reports[/b] discussion. Include:
[list]
[*]Your game version and the ZeD-GUI version (the desk's ZeD menu, About).
[*]Your mod list.
[*]What you did, what you expected, and what happened. Add a screenshot if you can.
[*]Your console.txt: [i]C:\Users\(you)\Zomboid\console.txt[/i] on Windows, [i]~/Zomboid/console.txt[/i] on Linux and macOS. Upload it to a paste site and post the link.
[/list]
[b]Safe mode:[/b] if ZeD-GUI stops you from playing, turn on Options, Mods, ZeD-GUI, Safe mode. The game's own screens return.

[img]IMG_BASE/h_requests_add_ons_and_translations.png[/img]
[list]
[*][b]Requests:[/b] the Requests discussion.
[*][b]Add-ons:[/b] the Add-on makers discussion has the guides. Watches can be added now.
[*][b]Translations:[/b] the Translations discussion. Translating needs text files only.
[/list]

[img]IMG_BASE/h_server_admins.png[/img]
Workshop ID: (after the first upload)
Mod ID: ZeD_UI
[code]WorkshopItems=(Workshop ID)
Mods=ZeD_UI\[/code]
Every player needs it, because it adds an item.

[img]IMG_BASE/h_credits.png[/img]
Made by Hermit. ZeD-GUI has been in development since Build 41 went stable. Every system, design and piece of logic was built to Hermit's vision. AI was used as a tool: Claude made it possible for one person to build a project that used to be out of scope for a solo modder. AI is the tool. Hermit is the maker.

Fonts: Fira Sans and Fira Mono (SIL Open Font License). Icons: sources and licenses are listed in the credits file.

Project Zomboid is made by The Indie Stone. ZeD-GUI is a fan-made mod built on the game's own systems, and is not affiliated with The Indie Stone or Apple.
